import editor/bim_editor_core.dl

function check arc wall {boolean:condition} named {string:label}:
    execute:
        if condition = false:
            print ((the string form of "FAIL: ") + label) as a line
            @intrinsic("call", "libc", "exit", nothing, 1)
        print ((the string form of "PASS: ") + label) as a line

function click arc wall at {cad vector2:point} in {a pointer to a bim editor record:editor}:
    execute:
        move bim editor pointer to point within 0.001 in editor
        press bim editor pointer in editor

set editor to a new bim editor
set e to the address of editor
set before to the length of (editor's documentValue's current's walls's values)
set editor's tool to bim arc wall tool
set editor's moveStage to 0
click arc wall at (a cad vector2 with x 20.0 and y 20.0) in e
click arc wall at (a cad vector2 with x 26.0 and y 20.0) in e
check arc wall ((the length of (editor's documentValue's current's walls's values)) = before) named (the string form of "two clicks leave the model unchanged")
click arc wall at (a cad vector2 with x 23.0 and y 20.0) in e
check arc wall ((the length of (editor's documentValue's current's walls's values)) = before) named (the string form of "collinear third point does not create a wall")
click arc wall at (a cad vector2 with x 23.0 and y 19.0) in e
check arc wall ((the length of (editor's documentValue's current's walls's values)) = (before + 1)) named (the string form of "three clicks create one native wall")
set made to the item at before in (editor's documentValue's current's walls's values)
check arc wall ((the absolute value of (made's bulge - 1.0)) < 1e-7) named (the string form of "wall arc passes through the third point")
check arc wall (editor's moveStage = 0) named (the string form of "ready to start another arc")
